"choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "\\(x<\\frac76\\)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "\\(x<\\frac68\\)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "\\(x<\\frac67\\) or \\(x>8\\)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "\\(x>7\\)"}, {"key": "E", "text": "\\(x>\\frac67\\) or \\(x<7\\)"}]}, "explanation": "If \\(x\\le7/4\\), then \\(|7-4x|=7-4x\\), so \\(7-4x>3x+1\\) gives \\(x<6/7\\). If \\(x>7/4\\), then \\(|7-4x|=4x-7\\), so \\(4x-7>3x+1\\) gives \\(x>8\\). The full solution is \\(x<6/7\\) or \\(x>8\\); the endpoints are excluded.", "correct": "C"}, {"id": "5cf35d24-e7fb-5083-17c9-e7dc4697a9de", "before": {"stem": "Question 21. If |7 −4𝑥| > 3𝑥+ 1, which of the following is the solution of the inequality?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "𝑥< 7\n 6"}, {"key": "B", "text": "𝑥< 6\n 8"}, {"key": "C", "text": "𝑥< 6 or 𝑥> 8\n 7"}, {"key": "D", "text": "𝑥> 7"}, {"key": "E", "text": "𝑥> 6 or 𝑥< 7\n 7\n\n 8\nESTII-HS Math L1 January 2026"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "For x<=7/4, 7-4x>3x+1 gives x<6/7. For x>=7/4, 4x-7>3x+1 gives x>8. Thus x<6/7 or x>8."}, "source_question_id": "est2_hs_level1_jan_2026-q00281", "source": "ESTII-HS Math L1 January 2026, physical page 8, Q21 (repeated on page 173)", "review_note": "Visually checked all five printed options; restored fraction grouping and removed page footer.", "release": true, "fields": {"stem": "Which is the solution of \\(|7-4x|>3x+1\\)?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "\\(x<\\frac76\\)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "\\(x<\\frac68\\)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "\\(x<\\frac67\\) or \\(x>8\\)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "\\(x>7\\)"}, {"key": "E", "text": "\\(x>\\frac67\\) or \\(x<7\\)"}]}, "explanation": "If \\(x\\le7/4\\), then \\(|7-4x|=7-4x\\), so \\(7-4x>3x+1\\) gives \\(x<6/7\\). If \\(x>7/4\\), then \\(|7-4x|=4x-7\\), so \\(4x-7>3x+1\\) gives \\(x>8\\). The full solution is \\(x<6/7\\) or \\(x>8\\); the endpoints are excluded.", "correct": "C"}, {"id": "0f0b042e-07b3-ed26-ff04-51e8fd399a9e", "before": {"stem": "Question 20. A spinner is divided into 12 sections labeled $0, $1, $2, $5, and $10, as shown\n in the figure above. If the spinner is spun twice and all sectors have equal\n probability of landing on the given arrow, what is the probability of obtaining a\n sum of 10?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1\n 36"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2\n 36"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4\n 36"}, {"key": "D", "text": "5\n 36"}, {"key": "E", "text": "7\n 36"}], "correct": "D", "explanation": "The spinner has four $5 sectors, one $0 sector and two $10 sectors among 12. Ordered pairs summing to $10 are 4*4 from 5+5 and 2*1*2 from 0+10, totaling 20/144=5/36."}, "source_question_id": "est2_hs_level1_jan_2026-q00020", "source": "ESTII-HS Math L1 January 2026, rendered page 8, Q20", "review_note": "Counted the actual sectors: one $0, four $1, one $2, four $5, two $10. Correct key D is independently confirmed despite the handwritten mark on C.", "release": true, "fields": {"stem": "A fair spinner has 12 equal sectors: one labeled $0, four labeled $1, one labeled $2, four labeled $5, and two labeled $10. It is spun twice independently. What is the probability that the two amounts sum to $10?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1/36"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2/36"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4/36"}, {"key": "D", "text": "5/36"}, {"key": "E", "text": "7/36"}]}, "explanation": "For a sum of $10, the spins must be $5 and $5, $0 then $10, or $10 then $0. The probability is \\((4/12)^2+2(1/12)(2/12)=20/144=5/36\\), choice D.", "correct": "D"}, {"id": "3441a517-54ce-99ae-888e-e47bc9befcaf", "before": {"stem": "Question 20. A spinner is divided into 12 sections labeled $0, $1, $2, $5, and $10, as shown\n in the figure above. If the spinner is spun twice and all sectors have equal\n probability of landing on the given arrow, what is the probability of obtaining a\n sum of 10?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1\n 36"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2\n 36"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4\n 36"}, {"key": "D", "text": "5\n 36"}, {"key": "E", "text": "7\n 36"}], "correct": "D", "explanation": "The spinner has four $5 sectors, one $0 sector and two $10 sectors among 12. Ordered pairs summing to $10 are 4*4 from 5+5 and 2*1*2 from 0+10, totaling 20/144=5/36."}, "source_question_id": "est2_hs_level1_jan_2026-q00280", "source": "ESTII-HS Math L1 January 2026, rendered page 8, Q20", "review_note": "Counted the actual sectors: one $0, four $1, one $2, four $5, two $10. Correct key D is independently confirmed despite the handwritten mark on C.", "release": true, "fields": {"stem": "A fair spinner has 12 equal sectors: one labeled $0, four labeled $1, one labeled $2, four labeled $5, and two labeled $10. It is spun twice independently. What is the probability that the two amounts sum to $10?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "1/36"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2/36"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4/36"}, {"key": "D", "text": "5/36"}, {"key": "E", "text": "7/36"}]}, "explanation": "For a sum of $10, the spins must be $5 and $5, $0 then $10, or $10 then $0. The probability is \\((4/12)^2+2(1/12)(2/12)=20/144=5/36\\), choice D.", "correct": "D"}, {"id": "f0fdb1f5-7e1f-5a4d-859b-80c47e1c9f48", "before": {"stem": "In the figure, d₁ and d₂ are two parallel lines. Which of the following is always true?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "z = x"}, {"key": "B", "text": "z = x − y"}, {"key": "C", "text": "x = y − z"}, {"key": "D", "text": "x + z + y = 180"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "The angle y is an exterior angle of the triangle formed with the upper parallel. It equals x + z, so x = y − z."}, "source_question_id": null, "source": "EST I Questions by Topic, GT009; original figure gt-009-1.png visually inspected", "review_note": "Verified angle positions and exterior-angle relationship in the source diagram.", "release": true, "fields": {}, "explanation": "Because the horizontal lines are parallel, the descending transversal makes the same acute angle \\(x\\) with either line. At the crossing, the left-hand angle \\(y\\) is the sum of the two acute inclinations: \\(y=x+z\\). Rearranging gives \\(x=y-z\\), choice C.", "correct": "C"}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
