2a-baed-1a9e8a5195c1", "before": {"stem": "Q51. Classes: 10-A (28), 10-B (25), 11-A (30), 11-B (24). Grade 10: 25% of 10-A and\n 32% of 10-B failed. Grade 11: 20% of 11-A and 50% of 11-B failed. What is the ratio\n of failing students in grade 11 to passing students in grade 10?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "8 : 15"}, {"key": "B", "text": "9 : 18"}, {"key": "C", "text": "9 : 19"}, {"key": "D", "text": "15 : 13\n\nAbdelrahman Ghoneem | 01116004434 | EST & SAT Math Page 44"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "Verified answer key; source and release checks completed."}, "source_question_id": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026-q00197", "source": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026; source page 44", "review_note": "Removed page-footer contamination; independently solved the complete problem and checked every choice.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "8 : 15"}, {"key": "B", "text": "9 : 18"}, {"key": "C", "text": "9 : 19"}, {"key": "D", "text": "15 : 13"}]}, "explanation": "Grade 11 failures total 0.20(30) + 0.50(24) = 6 + 12 = 18. Grade 10 passes total 0.75(28) + 0.68(25) = 21 + 17 = 38. The ratio is 18:38 = 9:19.", "correct": "C"}, {"id": "9d12bcad-39a9-566d-2296-08bc5685d78d", "before": {"stem": "Q23. Which equation represents a line that falls (decreases) as x increases?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "2x − 3y = 5"}, {"key": "B", "text": "y = 2x + 4"}, {"key": "C", "text": "−2x − 3y = 7"}, {"key": "D", "text": "y = 0.4x − 3\n\nAbdelrahman Ghoneem | 01116004434 | EST & SAT Math Page 6"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "Verified answer key; source and release checks completed."}, "source_question_id": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026-q00023", "source": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026; source page 6", "review_note": "Removed page-footer contamination; independently solved the complete problem and checked every choice.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "2x − 3y = 5"}, {"key": "B", "text": "y = 2x + 4"}, {"key": "C", "text": "−2x − 3y = 7"}, {"key": "D", "text": "y = 0.4x − 3"}]}, "explanation": "A line decreases as x increases exactly when its slope is negative. In C, −2x − 3y = 7 rearranges to y = −(2/3)x − 7/3. Its slope is −2/3. The other listed slopes are positive.", "correct": "C"}, {"id": "a0958a1f-6c86-37da-d562-375e86ac43b0", "before": {"stem": "Q30. Given 2y = 3x + 4, which of the following is a line perpendicular to it?", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "y = (3/2)x + 5"}, {"key": "B", "text": "5y = 2x − 5"}, {"key": "C", "text": "3y = −2x + 11"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2y = −3x + 10\n\nAbdelrahman Ghoneem | 01116004434 | EST & SAT Math Page 7"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "Verified answer key; source and release checks completed."}, "source_question_id": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026-q00029", "source": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026; source page 7", "review_note": "Removed page-footer contamination; independently solved the complete problem and checked every choice.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "y = (3/2)x + 5"}, {"key": "B", "text": "5y = 2x − 5"}, {"key": "C", "text": "3y = −2x + 11"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2y = −3x + 10"}]}, "explanation": "The given line has slope 3/2. A perpendicular line has slope −2/3. Choice C, 3y = −2x + 11, has that slope.", "correct": "C"}, {"id": "a3c46f8d-9002-0856-a12b-4b64937e932e", "before": {"stem": "Q105. Add: (−7p³q + 6pq) + (4p³q − 8pq + 3) + (7pq + 7).", "choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "−11p³q + 13pq + 10"}, {"key": "B", "text": "−3p³q + 21pq + 10"}, {"key": "C", "text": "−3p³q + 5pq + 10"}, {"key": "D", "text": "−4p³q + 5pq + 9\n\nAbdelrahman Ghoneem | 01116004434 | EST & SAT Math Page 21"}], "correct": "C", "explanation": "Verified answer key; source and release checks completed."}, "source_question_id": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026-q00103", "source": "ghoneem_full_revision_jun_2026; source page 21", "review_note": "Removed page-footer contamination; independently solved the complete problem and checked every choice.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [{"key": "A", "text": "−11p³q + 13pq + 10"}, {"key": "B", "text": "−3p³q + 21pq + 10"}, {"key": "C", "text": "−3p³q + 5pq + 10"}, {"key": "D", "text": "−4p³q + 5pq + 9"}]}, "explanation": "Combine like terms. The p³q coefficient is −7 + 4 = −3; the pq coefficient is 6 − 8 + 7 = 5; and the constants sum to 3 + 7 = 10. The result is −3p³q + 5pq + 10.", "correct": "C"}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
