nd use (2,5): 5 = 4 + b, giving b = 1.", "correct": [1]}, {"id": "c09a1ac8-37f7-4870-931b-64ac5fb657d2", "before": {"stem": "For the same two lines, \\(y=2x+1\\) and \\(y=-x+7\\), what is the value of \\(y\\) at the intersection point?", "choices": [], "correct": [5], "explanation": "At \\(x=2\\): \\(y=2(2)+1=5\\).<br><b>Desmos tip:</b> Read the second coordinate of the intersection point."}, "source_question_id": null, "source": "None; source page None", "review_note": "Both equations are explicit; removed unnecessary previous-question reference and checked the intersection.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [], "stem": "The lines y = 2x + 1 and y = −x + 7 intersect. What is the y-coordinate of the intersection?"}, "explanation": "At the intersection, 2x + 1 = −x + 7. Thus 3x = 6 and x = 2. Substituting gives y = 5.", "correct": [5]}, {"id": "e9e55add-82c7-4ddd-b49d-b72bc79d2de7", "before": {"stem": "For the same system, \\(3x+2y=12\\) and \\(x-y=1\\), what is the value of \\(y\\)? (Fraction or decimal.)", "choices": [], "correct": [1.8], "explanation": "\\(y=x-1=2.8-1=1.8\\).<br><b>Desmos tip:</b> Both coordinates appear when you click the intersection."}, "source_question_id": null, "source": "None; source page None", "review_note": "Both equations are explicit; removed unnecessary previous-question reference and solved by substitution.", "release": true, "fields": {"choices": [], "stem": "If 3x + 2y = 12 and x − y = 1, what is y? Enter a fraction or decimal."}, "explanation": "From x − y = 1, x = y + 1. Then 3(y + 1) + 2y = 12, so 5y = 9 and y = 9/5 = 1.8.", "correct": [1.8]}]$payload$::jsonb) LOOP
